    sisterModels: [ { name: "BMW 330e (G20)", note: "The incredibly popular G20 330e utilized the exact same B48 PHEV drivetrain, offering exceptional efficiency but suffering from the exact same incredibly expensive hybrid battery degradation risks." } ],
    tuningPotential: [
      { stage: "Stage 1 (Bootmod3 / MHD Flash)", power: "360 - 380 hp", notes: "The ultimate value upgrade. This 'O1' variant features a highly robust closed-deck block, and you can safely flash the internal combustion engine via the OBD port to unlock horsepower. However, tuning a PHEV is incredibly risky. The transmission and EME module are heavily stressed by the combined torque. If you flash this, you are taking a massive gamble on the hybrid system's lifespan.", zeroToHundred: "4.9s", hundredToTwoHundred: "13.0s" },
      { stage: "Stage 2 (Not Recommended)", power: "N/A", notes: "Requires a high-flow downpipe and an aggressive tune. While the B48 block handles this power effortlessly, pushing the hybrid powertrain to this level is highly discouraged. The ZF 8HP75PH transmission and the incredibly expensive electric motor are not designed to handle massive, sustained torque increases. You will likely destroy the gearbox.", zeroToHundred: "N/A", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" },
      { stage: "Stage 3 (Not Recommended)", power: "N/A", notes: "Attempting to bolt a massive hybrid turbocharger to the PHEV drivetrain is completely irrational and practically financial suicide. The complex interplay between the EME inverter, the electric motor, and the heavily tuned petrol engine will inevitably result in catastrophic failure.", zeroToHundred: "N/A", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" }
    ],
